h in Colesville, 28 August 1830", "editorialPageNumber": "135", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/26070/26070-0008.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> lion shall lie down with the lamb &amp;c. But brethren be not dis-couraged when we tell you of perilous times, for they must shortly come, for the sword, famine, and pestilence are approaching,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14001751993707000482\"><a href=\"#14001751993707000482\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans14\"><span id=\"documenttrans14\">14</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Jeremiah 14:12; 29:17–18; 44:13; and Ezekiel 6:11; 12:16.</p><hr></div></div></aside> for there shall be great destructions upon the face of this land,<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17201328868136305821\"><a href=\"#17201328868136305821\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans15\"><span id=\"documenttrans15\">15</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">A <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" poptitle=\"Revelation, September 1830–A [D&amp;C\n29]\">revelation</a> dated shortly after this letter was written reiterated this theme. (See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" poptitle=\"Revelation, September 1830–A [D&amp;C\n29]\">Revelation, Sept. 1830–A</a> [D&amp;C 29:9–11].)</p><hr></div></div></aside> for ye need not suppose that one jot or tittle of the prophecies of all the Holy Prophets shall fail, and there are many that remain to be fulfilled [p. 135]</div></body></html>", "expandedTex